codex
Step 0 supports a Track B family, not Track A. The paper’s Section 1 gives the exact mixed-graph reachability definition and explicitly identifies easy regimes (no pre-directed arcs, \(k=2\), and an \(n^{O(k)}\) XP algorithm); Section 2’s flip and stacked-flip gadgets enforce opposite/equal edge directions, while Theorem 1’s NP-completeness is only worst-case and does not justify hardness for a planted distribution. I’ll therefore use those native planar gadgets to encode a large GF(2) system: generic Gaussian elimination is efficient and will be disclosed/measured, while the generated complement-basis symmetry gives a much shorter no-tool route.
