codex
One last G8 audit found an additional representation symmetry worth covering: reversing an undirected edge’s stored endpoint order while toggling its bias leaves every induced orientation unchanged, and reflecting a flip component swaps its two outer roles. I’m strengthening `canonical_key` and the 20-seed relabelling test to normalize both, instead of relying only on vertex/list permutations.
