    29	
    30	## Problem and trust model
    31	
    32	[Beck, Blum, Kryven, Löffler, and Zink, *Planar Steiner Orientation is
    33	NP-complete*](https://arxiv.org/abs/1804.07496) asks whether the undirected edges
    34	of a mixed graph can be oriented so every ordered terminal pair has a directed
    35	path. Section 2's flip gadget forces two edge directions to be opposite; two
    36	stacked flips force the outer directions to agree. This generator samples a
    37	96-bit key first, assigns independent tags and endpoint biases, and constructs
    38	each gadget around that key. This is inverse generation: no generated instance
    39	is solved to obtain its planted certificate.
