    41	The answer is `[[0,c0],...,[95,c95]]`. Edge tags turn that key into a concrete
    42	orientation by an exact GF(2) inner product. Verification then runs ordinary
    43	graph reachability for every terminal pair and never reads `inst["answer"]`.
    44	
    45	## Why Track B, not Track A
    46	
    47	The paper's Theorem 1 is worst-case NP-completeness. It says nothing about this
    48	generated distribution. Section 1 also records polynomial algorithms when the
    49	input has no pre-directed arcs and when there are only two terminal pairs, plus
    50	an `n^{O(k)}` XP algorithm in the number of terminal pairs. Those facts rule out
    51	using the paper title as a distributional-hardness claim.
